WEBVTT

00:01.980 --> 00:11.860
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:25.000 --> 00:26.210
Dedenne, go!

00:35.620 --> 00:37.360
Dedenne, did you get the ball?

00:39.100 --> 00:39.380
Huh?

00:39.840 --> 00:40.930
What's wrong?

00:46.340 --> 00:47.520
Do you live around here?

00:48.190 --> 00:49.060
I'm Eureka.

00:49.440 --> 00:50.800
This is Dedenne...

00:51.310 --> 00:52.280
...and this here is Squishy.

00:52.730 --> 00:55.130
They're both Pokémon I'm keeping.

01:04.090 --> 01:05.390
I wonder what that was about.

01:07.700 --> 01:08.350
Eureka!

01:08.510 --> 01:09.670
We are setting off!

01:10.150 --> 01:10.880
Okay!

01:18.200 --> 01:23.890
Find Melecie!
Numelgon and Dedenne!!

01:24.980 --> 01:34.850
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

01:24.980 --> 01:34.850
Z

01:25.030 --> 01:29.340
As they head towards Miare City so that Satoshi can participate in the Kalos League,

01:29.790 --> 01:32.980
he and his friends make a stop at Numelgon's home.

01:34.050 --> 01:34.790
Whoa!

01:35.430 --> 01:37.010
We're here, Dedenne!

01:39.490 --> 01:42.790
Dedenne, you were excited to see Numelgon again, right?

01:44.770 --> 01:46.680
You two got along so well, after all.

01:47.520 --> 01:50.290
Numelgon will be happy to see Dedenne, too.

01:53.270 --> 01:55.580
I wonder if it's doing all right.

02:04.140 --> 02:05.030
Hello!

02:06.950 --> 02:09.060
Oh... If it isn't Satoshi-kun and his friends.

02:09.670 --> 02:11.480
Kenzo-san, it's been a while.

02:11.930 --> 02:13.060
Is Numelgon here?

02:14.970 --> 02:16.110
It's by the spring.

02:17.130 --> 02:19.820
Madatsubomi, go get Numelgon.

02:21.350 --> 02:22.320
Oh, it's fine.

02:22.930 --> 02:24.110
We'll go there ourselves.

02:24.800 --> 02:26.610
I see. I'm sure it'll be happy.

02:27.250 --> 02:27.660
Yeah.

02:36.420 --> 02:37.850
Numelgon!

02:41.120 --> 02:42.290
Hey!

02:54.850 --> 02:55.650
Numelgon!

02:58.580 --> 03:00.050
It's been a while!

03:00.050 --> 03:01.570
We finally meet again!

03:01.570 --> 03:03.230
Numelgon, have you been doing all right?

03:04.990 --> 03:07.080
The others seem the same as ever, too.

03:09.830 --> 03:10.720
Numelgon!

03:11.160 --> 03:13.260
This is my friend Squishy.

03:16.290 --> 03:17.250
Everyone, come out!

03:23.360 --> 03:25.760
Numelgon, some of them have evolved, too!

03:26.820 --> 03:28.300
You're meeting Onvern for the first time, right?

04:07.850 --> 04:08.790
Did something happen?

04:12.580 --> 04:13.380
Hey, stop!

04:19.670 --> 04:20.200
That's...

04:20.760 --> 04:22.450
Oh, it's the little one we ran into earlier!

04:23.700 --> 04:25.550
Melecie, the Jewel Pokémon.

04:25.960 --> 04:32.500
It is said to have been born from high pressures and temperatures underground. Its body is as hard as diamond.

04:33.070 --> 04:34.510
Why would you do this?

04:37.020 --> 04:38.620
So many Melecie!

04:38.980 --> 04:41.790
They usually live in caves deep underground...

04:42.710 --> 04:43.800
Why would they come up to the surface?

04:47.640 --> 04:48.840
Are they friends, maybe?

04:55.580 --> 04:56.190
Eureka!

05:05.920 --> 05:07.080
It's gone!

05:11.750 --> 05:13.440
Hey, hey! Calm down!

05:13.980 --> 05:15.840
Are you friends with the little one from earlier?

05:23.830 --> 05:25.220
Satoshi, what should we do?

05:25.780 --> 05:27.890
What we should do...?

05:28.330 --> 05:30.300
It's not like we can just leave them to their own devices, so...

05:31.190 --> 05:31.600
All right.

05:32.250 --> 05:34.700
Let's all split up and look for the Melecie from earlier.

05:34.970 --> 05:35.740
Agreed.

05:42.160 --> 05:43.150
Thanks, everyone.

05:44.120 --> 05:45.180
Now that that's decided...

05:45.480 --> 05:47.760
Fiarrow, Onvern, I choose you.

05:51.470 --> 05:52.870
Please look for Melecie.

05:57.760 --> 06:01.610
Horubee, use Dig to search for Melecie from underground.

06:05.120 --> 06:06.470
All right, we're counting on you guys as well!

06:06.890 --> 06:07.860
Yeah!

06:13.820 --> 06:15.020
Melecie!

06:15.420 --> 06:17.550
Stop hiding and come out!

06:20.430 --> 06:21.840
Dedenne, anything over there?

06:28.310 --> 06:28.840
Horubee!

07:21.450 --> 07:23.500
What's that Pokémon that keeps thrashing about?

07:24.010 --> 07:25.320
It's a Melecie.

07:26.020 --> 07:26.890
Melecie...

07:27.590 --> 07:28.880
It's the Jewel Pokémon.

07:28.880 --> 07:29.920
"Jewel Pokémon"?!

07:30.770 --> 07:32.240
Oh... But...

07:34.060 --> 07:35.880
I can't possibly...

07:36.700 --> 07:38.980
...turn such a big Pokémon into a ring...

07:39.910 --> 07:41.890
...and even as an earring...

07:42.780 --> 07:45.110
...it'd just hurt my earlobe pretty badly.

07:45.570 --> 07:46.700
Oh, maybe a tiara?

07:47.430 --> 07:47.780
Nope.

07:48.160 --> 07:49.400
Super ugly.

07:51.700 --> 07:52.850
It's useless.

07:53.180 --> 07:56.380
But its body is said to be as hard as diamond.

07:56.880 --> 07:57.800
Uh-huh...

07:58.330 --> 08:00.260
That's kinda neat info!

08:00.630 --> 08:01.280
I've decided!

08:03.510 --> 08:05.070
That's a good idea!

08:05.070 --> 08:06.670
Let's get started right away.

08:07.000 --> 08:07.860
Roger!

08:43.240 --> 08:44.330
How'd you guys do?

08:49.790 --> 08:50.710
No luck, huh?

08:53.220 --> 08:55.100
Could it have gone farther away?

08:55.630 --> 08:56.960
Let's expand the search area.

08:57.770 --> 08:59.050
Fiarrow, Onvern!

09:02.470 --> 09:03.780
All right.

09:04.270 --> 09:05.340
First comes...

09:06.810 --> 09:07.420
...the mecha.

09:11.430 --> 09:13.580
Aren't these Melecie?

09:14.810 --> 09:16.520
There's so many of them, too.

09:17.580 --> 09:18.150
Nyarth,

09:18.770 --> 09:19.400
translate.

09:20.070 --> 09:22.150
Uh... In short,

09:22.840 --> 09:29.160
it seems a friend they'd been living with disappeared off somewhere and they're all looking for it right now.

09:30.940 --> 09:33.390
Could that be the one we saw...?

09:33.570 --> 09:34.860
But it went undergr-

09:34.860 --> 09:37.570
Oh, <i>that</i> Melecie!

09:37.570 --> 09:39.200
We know where it is.

09:40.750 --> 09:42.950
Hey, what are you planning to do?

09:45.080 --> 09:48.350
We'll make use of all of them.

09:49.240 --> 09:51.120
Let's hurry up and change the number of arms to six.

09:55.400 --> 09:56.680
Pokémon Quiz.

09:56.680 --> 09:57.280
The answer...

09:57.280 --> 09:58.380
...is...?

09:59.890 --> 10:09.910
Coming up next:

09:59.890 --> 10:04.860
The Melecie are in big trouble!!

10:00.870 --> 10:05.560
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

10:04.930 --> 10:09.910
What is the Rocket Gang's new mecha model!?

11:20.440 --> 11:21.730
Where have you gone?

11:24.990 --> 11:26.410
You've found Melecie, huh?

11:30.050 --> 11:31.010
Eureka, let's go!

11:31.790 --> 11:32.120
Yeah.

11:32.730 --> 11:34.610
Dedenne, Squishy, hold on ti...

11:35.910 --> 11:36.380
Huh?

11:36.790 --> 11:37.960
Squishy, where's Dedenne?

11:42.830 --> 11:43.880
So you have found it!

11:52.950 --> 11:53.700
Ah, there it is!

11:55.810 --> 11:57.240
Thank goodness we've found you.

11:58.520 --> 12:00.360
Your friends were looking for y...

12:01.360 --> 12:02.810
Uh... Huh? Where are they?

12:07.630 --> 12:08.280
Where is Eureka?

12:14.790 --> 12:15.190
Okay!

12:16.240 --> 12:17.090
It's done!

12:17.540 --> 12:20.720
Now we just need to set the Melecie.

12:47.940 --> 12:49.000
Ah, this is...!

12:49.250 --> 12:50.800
It's the mini brat girl's Dedenne!

12:51.750 --> 12:53.160
We won't let you get in the way.

12:53.570 --> 12:55.950
Go, Pumpjin! Shadow Ball!

12:59.050 --> 13:00.610
Go, Maaiika!

13:00.880 --> 13:01.930
Psybeam!

13:09.270 --> 13:11.830
Dedenne! Dedenne!

13:12.130 --> 13:13.670
Where have you gone?

13:14.870 --> 13:15.580
Dedenne?

13:15.890 --> 13:17.640
Uh, hey! What's going on?

13:21.110 --> 13:23.120
They were with us a moment ago.

13:23.910 --> 13:26.030
I am sure they have not gone far yet.

13:26.310 --> 13:27.730
Bro!

13:27.350 --> 13:27.730
Eureka!

13:28.370 --> 13:29.370
Where have you been?

13:29.740 --> 13:31.870
This isn't the time to talk about that!

13:32.700 --> 13:33.570
Wh-What?!

13:45.580 --> 13:46.710
You guys again!

13:48.580 --> 13:50.710
If you tell us "You guys again!",

13:51.080 --> 13:53.010
It is the world's mercy that makes us answer!

13:53.720 --> 13:55.510
To prevent the world's destruction!

13:56.140 --> 13:58.240
To protect the world's peace!

13:58.490 --> 14:01.110
Carrying out the evil of love and truth,

14:01.590 --> 14:04.020
we're lovely, charmy villains!

14:05.140 --> 14:05.800
Musashi!

14:06.190 --> 14:06.570
Kojiro!

14:07.140 --> 14:09.970
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

14:10.230 --> 14:12.890
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

14:13.090 --> 14:14.650
Just kidding!

14:17.290 --> 14:18.630
What's up with this mecha?!

14:19.510 --> 14:21.460
When she asked, "What's up with this mecha?!",

14:21.770 --> 14:26.750
I replied, "It's a mecha that has Melecie, who're hard as diamonds, attached to the tip of its arms".

14:28.340 --> 14:30.630
Its name is "Hard Melecie Robo"!

14:42.290 --> 14:42.930
Ha!

14:48.020 --> 14:48.650
Take this!

14:51.370 --> 14:54.150
Whoa! They're as hard as diamond all right!

14:54.150 --> 14:55.860
What amazing power!

15:04.840 --> 15:06.530
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

15:14.740 --> 15:16.930
We're perfectly protected against electricity!

15:22.670 --> 15:24.770
Brute force won't work on us either!

15:41.920 --> 15:43.350
Melecie, Numelgon...

15:43.980 --> 15:45.160
Did you get an idea?

15:47.890 --> 15:50.230
What are you plotting?

15:50.230 --> 15:51.510
We're up for the challenge.

16:05.040 --> 16:07.390
Oh, right! A <i>Melecie</i> can take on a Melecie!

16:18.450 --> 16:19.770
Ah, it's so frail...

16:20.020 --> 16:23.580
Well, a Melecie's body <i>is</i> as hard as diamond...

16:50.810 --> 16:52.650
In that case, we'll use force!

16:53.050 --> 16:54.850
Pumpjin, Shadow Ball!

16:55.270 --> 16:56.360
Psybeam!

17:05.110 --> 17:05.740
Psybeam!

17:12.800 --> 17:14.160
Well done, Numelgon.

17:14.610 --> 17:15.920
Dragon Pulse!

17:24.570 --> 17:25.130
All right!

17:27.130 --> 17:28.980
Numelgon, Ice Beam!

17:34.550 --> 17:37.380
Aw... I thought it was a good mecha...

17:38.100 --> 17:40.010
And it had tough defense, too...

17:40.790 --> 17:42.890
This feels bad!

17:54.240 --> 17:55.380
They're making up!

17:56.610 --> 17:58.120
I guess this case is closed now.

17:58.420 --> 17:58.900
Right?

17:59.500 --> 17:59.940
Yeah.

18:00.570 --> 18:01.660
Thank goodness.

18:10.790 --> 18:11.490
Don't worry about it.

18:12.100 --> 18:13.650
Don't cause trouble for the others any more, okay?

18:19.030 --> 18:20.240
Be careful!

18:20.240 --> 18:21.400
Take care!

18:35.370 --> 18:36.410
Take this! And this!

18:38.080 --> 18:38.930
And this!

18:39.870 --> 18:40.580
This!

18:47.580 --> 18:49.270
Awesome, Dedenne!

18:55.090 --> 18:58.560
Everyone, make sure to rest well before the League, now.

18:59.190 --> 19:00.440
It is going to be soon, after all.

19:01.020 --> 19:04.680
All right, let's go give it our all and win the Kalos League!

19:10.540 --> 19:11.310
Got it.

19:11.780 --> 19:12.690
We'll make sure to win, promise.

19:15.490 --> 19:21.300
An unexpected incident at Numelgon's home has safely been resolved thanks to Satoshi and his friends' efforts.

19:22.740 --> 19:26.540
All right. Next time, the Kalos League will finally begin!

19:27.280 --> 19:28.200
To be continued.

19:42.760 --> 19:43.350
It's strong.

19:44.080 --> 19:45.600
Lucario is unable to battle.

19:46.130 --> 19:48.110
Therefore, the challenger wins!

19:59.100 --> 20:01.200
This is proof that you have won at the Shala Gym:

20:01.870 --> 20:02.720
The Fight Badge.

20:06.170 --> 20:07.220
This is your eighth, right?

20:07.840 --> 20:09.020
You'll be participating, won't you? In the League, I mean.

20:10.070 --> 20:10.310
Yeah.

20:11.150 --> 20:12.640
There's someone there I want to fight.

20:13.560 --> 20:14.970
I hope you get matched up with them, then.

20:15.970 --> 20:17.410
They're quite strong.

20:18.590 --> 20:20.220
I'm sure they'll fight their way up.

20:26.700 --> 20:28.250
The latest news on the movie!

20:29.300 --> 20:33.750
Right now, special Volcanion battle videos filled with techniques...

20:34.140 --> 20:36.950
...that make you stronger than anyone else are being streamed on the official movie website!

20:37.910 --> 20:41.430
You make Volcanion, which you can only obtain with the special pre-order ticket, your partner...

20:41.900 --> 20:44.740
...and aim to be the strongest Pokémon Trainer as well!

20:45.600 --> 20:46.210
Also...

20:47.390 --> 20:49.960
We will now reveal the final results of the Pokémon Elections 720...

20:50.330 --> 20:53.750
...that determines the Pokémon that will be given away in theaters.

20:55.320 --> 20:58.870
The one who won against the fierce competition and claimed the glorious title is...

21:00.550 --> 21:02.940
...the Ninja Pokémon Gekkouga!

21:03.600 --> 21:07.340
Gekkouga, who also plays a huge role in the anime as Satoshi's partner,

21:07.840 --> 21:10.610
will be given away at theaters for your games!

21:11.610 --> 21:15.980
Incredible! It comes with a very special held item: The ultimate ball, the Master Ball!

21:16.660 --> 21:20.910
Premieres Saturday July 16th!

21:16.870 --> 21:20.260
Watch the movie and obtain the Gekkouga you've all chosen!

21:20.910 --> 21:25.900
Sunday June 12th at 8am!

21:21.810 --> 21:25.230
As part of his voice actor training, Abareru-kun becomes an Onigohri!

21:22.310 --> 21:24.360
That hurts! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

21:24.560 --> 21:25.490
Ow! Ow!

21:28.080 --> 21:29.990
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:30.190 --> 21:31.310
Towards our next adventure!

21:32.390 --> 21:33.170
Ingenuities...

21:33.360 --> 21:34.380
...mean romance!

21:34.810 --> 21:37.270
They're the fruits of humans' wits and creativity!

21:37.820 --> 21:43.800
At the Ingenuity Festival, people from all over Kalos who're proud of their skills will come to present a selection of their ingenuities...!

21:37.970 --> 21:38.950
Bro!

21:44.570 --> 21:47.530
Woo! I cannot contain my excitement!

21:47.060 --> 21:50.250
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:50.500 --> 21:52.690
Heatbursts at the Ingenuity Festival!

21:52.360 --> 21:55.810
Next Time

21:52.360 --> 21:55.810
Heatbursts at the Ingenuity Festival!

21:53.170 --> 21:55.270
Everyone, get Pokémon!

21:55.850 --> 22:05.900
Next episode:

21:55.850 --> 22:00.830
Citron is extremely excited!

21:56.740 --> 22:01.310
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

22:00.860 --> 22:05.900
Go to the Ingenuity Festival!
